{"ts":"2026-07-31T06:03:48.007Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"bbccd5ce4f6ac18346c324e7","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Measured 2026-07-31 at HEAD across nineteen read surfaces\n\nThe published extraction contract is `.row_contract.jq_selector`, whose value on every surface that emits it is:\n\n```\n.row_contract.row_keys[] as $key | .[$key][]?\n```\n\nThat expression is a pure function of `row_keys`. When `row_keys` is empty or absent, it yields nothing — always, regardless of what the envelope actually contains.\n\n| class | surfaces | count |\n|---|---|---|\n| contract usable (`row_keys` populated) | list, search, history, activity, health, next, context | 7 |\n| contract present but vacuous (`row_keys: []` or absent, selector still published) | deps, stats, aggregate, get | 4 |\n| no `row_contract` at all | comments, notes, files, docs, graph, contracts, validate | 7 |\n| no envelope (NDJSON stream, no contract possible) | events | 1 |\n\n## The defect this item owns\n\nThe middle class. `pm deps pm-doxj --json` emits:\n\n```\n\"row_contract\": {\"command\":\"deps\",\"row_keys\":[],\"fields\":\"unsupported\",\n                 \"jq_selector\":\".row_contract.row_keys[] as $key | .[$key][]?\"}\n```\n\nThe item has 18 dependency edges. The published selector returns zero rows. `pm stats --json` behaves identically while carrying `by_type` and `by_status` collections.\n\nA missing contract fails loudly: the agent sees `null`, knows the surface is not covered, and special-cases it. A vacuous contract fails silently: the agent runs the documented one-liner, gets an empty stream, and cannot distinguish \"this surface never populates row_keys\" from \"the query matched nothing\". Silence is the worse failure because it is indistinguishable from a legitimate empty result, and every downstream count, loop and guard reads zero.\n\n## Relationship to the general row-contract programme\n\n`pm-sb0tns` owns the general problem — that no single shell or jq expression works across pm — and its acceptance criteria already require a documented one-liner exercised by a test, and require surfaces that cannot project fields to state why. This item is the narrow, immediately fixable subset: a surface that declares `fields: \"unsupported\"` and carries no row keys must not also publish a selector that is guaranteed to return nothing. Either it names its real row collection, or it omits `jq_selector` so the absence is visible.\n\nThis is not a request to make every surface projectable. It is a request that the self-describing contract never describe itself falsely.\n\n## Minimal correct shape\n\n- A surface that has row collections populates `row_keys` with their real key names, even when `--fields` is unsupported. `deps` has `nodes` and `edges`; `stats` has its count maps; `aggregate` has its groups.\n- A surface with genuinely no row collection omits `jq_selector` entirely, or sets it to a value the contract defines as \"no rows on this surface\".\n- A gate asserts the invariant directly: for every read command, if `row_contract.jq_selector` is present then evaluating it against the same envelope must return the same row count the envelope actually contains. That is checkable without knowing anything about the individual command."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-x710qm"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Four read surfaces publish a jq_selector that is guaranteed to return nothing: the self-describing row contract is present, vacuous, and indistinguishable from an empty result"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"deps, stats, aggregate and get emit the universal jq_selector with row_keys empty, so the documented extraction one-liner silently yields zero rows on surfaces that demonstrably have rows."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ergonomics","composability","contracts","pm-cli","token-efficiency"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-31T06:03:48.007Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-31T06:03:48.007Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"No read surface publishes a jq_selector that cannot return the rows its envelope contains; Surfaces with row collections populate row_keys with the real key names even when --fields is unsupported; A gate evaluates each read command envelope against its own published selector and asserts the returned row count matches the envelope contents; Surfaces that emit no envelope at all (the NDJSON event stream) are declared as such in the contract documentation rather than discovered by a parser returning null"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Makes the one published extraction expression trustworthy, which is the precondition for every shell and jq workflow the product advertises."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"The composability principle promises grep/jq pipelines; a contract that lies by returning empty is worse for a scripted agent than no contract at all."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-mpbb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"If a read surface publishes jq_selector, evaluating it returns the rows the envelope contains."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"deps (18 edges), stats, aggregate and get publish the selector with row_keys empty; it returns zero rows on all four."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"cli/read-surfaces"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"451e44e1fd5a424c0e09a066686057a503c185875b03c36512bfae6e674b4fa5","message":"Filed from a 2026-07-31 ecosystem planning pass: measured across 19 read surfaces at HEAD"}
